{
  "_notes": [
    "Danish-specific decisions worth knowing before editing this file:",
    "- 'ton' is mapped to metric_ton (1000 kg), NOT pint's bare 'ton' (US short ton, 907 kg) - matches everyday Danish usage.",
    "- 'pund' is NOT mapped at all - traditional Danish pund is exactly 500 g, not the imperial pound (453.6 g).",
    "- 'mil' is NOT mapped - the Scandinavian mile (10 km) is not the English mile.",
    "- 'hk'/'hestekraft' maps to metric_horsepower, NOT bare 'horsepower' (~1.4% different).",
    "- bare 'grader' only means angle (degree), never temperature - 'celsius'/'fahrenheit'/'kelvin' must be said explicitly."
